art without feeling left behind. During the afternoon, the team checked how things were going. They did not assume that silence meant success. They asked people directly and made another small adjustment when it was needed.","By the end of the afternoon, Orchard Classroom felt different. The original problem had become a chance to practise being careful. Amira returned a notebook to the table and wrote a note for the next group: “Check, listen, try, then improve.” The organiser thanked everyone, including the visitor whose question had changed the plan. Amira was pleased, but the best part was knowing how the group had reached its answer. They had not needed one person to know everything. They had needed people who were willing to think together."],"questions":[{"prompt":"What difficulty did the group face?","choices":["a box of donated objects had lost its labels","the planned activity left quieter visitors with no way to join","a delivery was delayed on the morning of an event","the first design kept falling over"],"correct":0,"explanation":"The organiser explains this difficulty on page 1.","hint":"Look back at what the group actually did."},{"prompt":"What did the group decide to do?","choices":["invite people to choose how they wanted to take part","write labels that explained where each object came from","adapt the activity instead of cancelling it","widen the base and test the design again"],"correct":1,"explanation":"The revised solution is described on page 3.","hint":"Look back at what the group actually did."},{"prompt":"Why did the group test a small version first?","choices":["To discover problems before using the full plan","To avoid listening to visitors","To make the task last forever","To hide the decision"],"correct":0,"explanation":"The trial let the group see what to improve before everyone arrived.","hint":"Think about what the trial revealed."}]}'::jsonb) ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET data=excluded.data;
