ped the newcomer take part without feeling left behind. During the afternoon, the team checked how things were going. They did not assume that silence meant success. They asked people directly and made another small adjustment when it was needed.","By the end of the afternoon, Lighthouse Reading Room felt different. The original problem had become a chance to practise being resourceful. Jules returned a checklist to the table and wrote a note for the next group: “Check, listen, try, then improve.” The organiser thanked everyone, including the visitor whose question had changed the plan. Jules was pleased, but the best part was knowing how the group had reached its answer. They had not needed one person to know everything. They had needed people who were willing to think together."],"questions":[{"prompt":"What difficulty did the group face?","choices":["two posters gave different opening times","the first design kept falling over","a delivery was delayed on the morning of an event","two groups wanted to use the same space"],"correct":2,"explanation":"The organiser explains this difficulty on page 1.","hint":"Look back at what the group actually did."},{"prompt":"What did the group decide to do?","choices":["agree a timetable that gave each group a turn","widen the base and test the design again","replace the old poster with a clear new notice","adapt the activity instead of cancelling it"],"correct":3,"explanation":"The revised solution is described on page 3.","hint":"Look back at what the group actually did."},{"prompt":"Why did the group test a small version first?","choices":["To discover problems before using the full plan","To avoid listening to visitors","To make the task last forever","To hide the decision"],"correct":0,"explanation":"The trial let the group see what to improve before everyone arrived.","hint":"Think about what the trial revealed."}]}'::jsonb) ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET data=excluded.data;
